s the g4 square (hxg4 would lose the bishop).\n4. **N: c6-d4**: This attacks the center but the square d4 is defended by White's pawn at e3 (exd4 would lose the knight).\n\nReason: Castling immediately ensures the King's safety and completes the opening phase. It removes potential targets for White and allows Black to focus on utilizing the central space advantage without worrying about the King. There are no immediate tactics to win material, so the principled strategic move is best.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
