 prepares for potential queenside expansion with b7-b5 in the future. Other moves like Be6 allow Nb5, which gives White unnecessary counterplay.\n\nReason: It restricts the opponent's only active plan for their Knight, preserves the strong Bishop pair, and maintains a solid positional advantage.\n\nAnswer: P: a7-a6"}
